# Cloudflare Pages redirects. Parsed by Pages, never served as a file.
# Host-level rules (www → apex) are not possible here: use a Bulk Redirect or a
# Redirect Rule in the dashboard, see SITE.md.

# No rule for /install.sh on purpose: site/install.sh is a real file here and
# is served from this origin, so
#
#   curl -fsSL https://abylab.ai/install.sh | bash
#
# still works on networks where raw.githubusercontent.com is blocked. It used
# to 302 to GitHub, which defeated the point — and a redirect beats the file,
# so re-adding one would silently hide the copy. site/install.sh is a
# byte-identical copy of the repo's install.sh; CI fails when the two drift.
